cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Please also cite the PGS Catalog, the PGS005206 publication and the
  source GWAS listed in the README when using the included data.
type: software
title: "PRSWeave: Adaptive Multi-Agent Orchestration for Polygenic Risk Research"
version: 0.1.0.dev0
abstract: >-
  PRSWeave (Polygenic Risk Score Workflow for Evidence, Adaptation,
  Validation, and Evaluation) is a research prototype for studying adaptive, evidence-grounded
  orchestration of polygenic risk score (PRS) workflows. Adaptive multi-agent
  orchestration is the long-term research architecture. Version 0.1 implements
  an LLM-driven Planner that coordinates deterministic scientific specialists,
  with an independent deterministic Validation Critic, a hash-chained audit
  log and pre-registered experiments on synthetic genotypes. It is not
  intended for clinical use.
